,"closed_at":"2025-09-18T17:13:14Z"},"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-08-19T23:38:12Z","updated_at":"2025-08-25T14:56:40Z","closed_at":"2025-08-25T14:56:36Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/109790","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109790","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109790.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109790.patch","merged_at":"2025-08-25T14:56:36Z"},"body":"This PR changes the way how we reset the audio position position tracking for the Web platform.\r\n\r\nPreviously, we based the logic around the [`AudioWorkletNode.port`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AudioWorkletNode/port) message handler setup in the constructor. That handler received \"reset\" messages and reset the `this.position` to `0`. Unfortunately, it seems that only Firefox truly is compatible with that method.\r\n\r\nI pivoted instead to use the native `AudioParam` support in [`AudioWorkletNode.parameters`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/AudioWorkletNode/parameters) in order to handle the position reset.\r\n\r\nThese params are usually for gain or other audio parameters. But I figured that I could send a \"reset\" value for the exact start frame, and sending a \"no reset\" value for every other frame. Now, on each processed frame, it checks if the \"reset\" property is bigger than 0, and if it is, it resets the position.\r\n\r\nFixes #109144 (hopefully)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109790/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109790/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}